{"id": "P00048", "name": "Liang Wenfeng", "name_chinese": "梁文锋", "country": "China", "net_worth_usd_m": "46140.4", "net_worth_source": "Forbes real-time", "source_of_wealth": "AI; hedge fund", "industry": "technology", "sec_insider_companies": "", "shared_with": "", "appears_on": "Forbes real-time (2026); Forbes annual (2025); Hurun China (2026); Hurun Unicorn founders (2026)", "focus": ["data_center_ai"], "forbes_profile_url": "https://www.forbes.com/profile/liang-wenfeng/", "wikidata_url": "", "forbes_bio": ["Liang Wenfeng is the founder of Hangzhou, China-based AI firm DeepSeek and quantitative trading firm High-Flyer Capital Management.", "DeepSeek took the world by storm when it released its R1 model in 2025, claiming to rival the performance of OpenAI's ChatGPT at a lower cost.", "Liang launched DeepSeek in 2023 and funded it in part with proceeds from High-Flyer, the hedge fund he founded in 2015 with two college classmates.", "The mogul used math and AI techniques to build High-Flyer, turning it into one of the country's largest and best-performing quantitative trading firms.", "DeepSeek raised $7.4 billion in a funding round in June 2026, valuing it at $52 billion."], "forbes_facts": ["Liang met with Chinese president Xi Jinping at a meeting with Chinese tech entrepreneurs in Beijing in 2025."]}
